# Copy this file to ".env" and fill it in. ".env" is git-ignored.
#
# ONLY public client values belong here. Both of these are designed to be
# visible in the browser; what protects your data is Row Level Security in the
# database and server-side Edge Functions, not hiding these.
#
# NEVER put the Supabase service_role / sb_secret_ key, database password,
# personal access token (sbp_), or Paystack secret key (sk_test_/sk_live_) here.
# `scripts/set-env.mjs` refuses to build if any secret key is found in .env.
# Server secrets go strictly to Supabase Edge Functions via `supabase secrets set`.

# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL
SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys → Publishable key (sb_publishable_...)
# (Recommended over legacy anon JWT; set either SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Legacy fallback if you still use the JWT anon key:
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
